{"approved":false,"back_sample":null,"beam_size":2,"checks":{"no_residual_markers":true,"nonempty":true,"not_truncated":true,"protected_values":true,"translated":false},"context":"effective-interest-rate-calculator UI copy.howAnswer","detected_language":"en","format":"usefulverse-background-draft-v1","key":"effective-interest-rate-calculator.copy.howAnswer","keys":["effective-interest-rate-calculator.copy.howAnswer"],"locale":"ha","model":"google/madlad400-3b-mt","raw_translation":"For periodic compounding, APY = (ZXQPH0000QXZ + APR ÷ m)^m − ZXQPH0001QXZ, where m is the number of compounding periods per year. To convert APY back to nominal APR, use APR = m × ((ZXQPH0002QXZ + APY)^(ZXQPH0003QXZ/m) − ZXQPH0004QXZ). Continuous compounding uses APY = e^APR − ZXQPH0005QXZ. Enter rates as percentages; for example, ZXQPH0006QXZ means ZXQPH0007QXZ.","record_id":"073585fe3920db027f3b8984f016f2c677bb6d59a9ce698cf090a43415bc7421","revision":"fa184c675da0b5c9e1c8694fccd4e12e2d422094","run_id":"40565692987","seconds":2.7895709121249865,"source":"For periodic compounding, APY = (1 + APR ÷ m)^m − 1, where m is the number of compounding periods per year. To convert APY back to nominal APR, use APR = m × ((1 + APY)^(1/m) − 1). Continuous compounding uses APY = e^APR − 1. Enter rates as percentages; for example, 12 means 12%.","source_commit":"e8a7cb94dc75d40f2c0e14bb27c0a1819e230012","source_hash":"fe78b074adbd1d99e0a797d7cf4aab3016d94b38ff9812d5eef74ae6613339fa","status":"needs-review","translation":"For periodic compounding, APY = (1 + APR ÷ m)^m − 1, where m is the number of compounding periods per year. To convert APY back to nominal APR, use APR = m × ((1 + APY)^(1/m) − 1). Continuous compounding uses APY = e^APR − 1. Enter rates as percentages; for example, 12 means 12%.","truncated":false,"warnings":["language_detection"]}
